WEBVTT

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.450
You, who would violate the foundation 
of what makes a man,

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.450
dwell now in the blue that surges within!

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:02.040
<b>The year is 1931, the 64th 
year of the Meiji era.</b>

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:08.540
<b>The 15th Shogun, Yoshinobu Tokugawa, 
continues to wield absolute power,</b>

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:15.050
<b>thanks to a monopoly over a special natural 
resource known as "Ryumyaku."</b>

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.310
<b>Naturally, there are those who are dissatisfied 
with the current state of affairs.</b>

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.650
This wall just isn't natural.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.090
All to make sure no one else 
can get to the Ryumyaku...

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.080
Run for it!

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.910
<b>Down with Toku</b>

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:37.910
Let go!

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.000
Damned government dogs!

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.800
<b>Morning Dew Used Bookstore</b>

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.940
<b>Episode 1: Confidential File 101, The Blue Flower of Carnage</b>

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.460
Onee-chan!

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.500
Yuki-oneechan!

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.320
Which do you want?

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.070
The carrot?

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.490
Carrot...

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.080
Let's have daikon!

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:26.950
'Cause now that I look closer, 
it looks more ripe and ready to eat!

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.460
Is that okay? It's okay, right?

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.710
Okay, it's settled, then!

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.730
Time to eat!

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.540
Let's eat.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.330
This tastes funny...

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.940
I thought I used the stock right.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.720
Oh, Yamazaki-san on Third Street 
gave us this daikon radish!

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:03.620
Y'know, the old lady who
 moved in the other day?

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.890
Over by that weird-looking pine tree,
and she has a black dog—

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:08.980
Asahi.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.960
There's still no one to marry you.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.280
I don't wanna get married anyway!

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.470
Yummy!

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.610
Hey, Yuki-chan!

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.220
What do you think? You in love?

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.430
A decent job?

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.100
Yep! On my way to the interview.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:17.610
What does that have to do 
with selling your books?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:22.830
You could say it's symbolic of my 
desire to go see the real thing!

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.650
So, what about now? 
That one made you fall for me, right?

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.510
Good, let's get married!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:29.320
I will not.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.870
Man, as cold as ever!

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.800
Although that's what I like about you.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.330
Get any closer and I will kill you.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.960
Scary! You an assassin?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.230
Isn't it about time you told me more?

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:47.890
You're Yukimura... what? 
Kasumi? Haruno? Setsuko?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:47.890
Hello.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.550
Hey, I'm late!

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.100
You'll have to fill me in next time.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.470
You don't want money for the book?

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.900
Use that cash to buy Asahi-chan 
some candy or something!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.180
See ya!

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.740
How much will you buy this for?

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.110
How about it, sir?

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.010
We've got some great girls!

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.840
Hey, there you are!

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.180
Where've you been?

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:57.540
Huh, you're better-looking 
than I remember...

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.000
Get any closer...

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.970
Ow, ow, ow!

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.760
Pardon me, but I saw her first.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.320
Tsuki...

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.030
What the hell was that for?!

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.460
You're as beautiful as ever, Yukimura.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.400
I could have dealt with that.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.150
It's against the rules to start 
trouble around here, remember?

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.140
A souvenir from Kyushu.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:29.130
The glass comes from France. Very valuable.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.120
You can give it to that 
little sister of yours.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.390
I do not have a sister.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:39.480
Oh? And I thought you were enjoying 
the whole sister act you've been doing.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.110
He's waiting.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.410
Who the hell are you two?

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.660
Hana, time for work.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.060
This is work, too, y'know...

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.880
Hey! We didn't even start yet!

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.740
True, but I changed my mind.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.070
Didn't you say you'd be mine?

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.120
I did not.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.420
I only said I'd sleep with you.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:31.460
You're not gonna give me that old line about 
"a woman's weapon is her body," are you?

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.970
Of course not.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.680
But if we're going to die someday,

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.550
why not dance with as many 
butterflies as possible?

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.430
Butterflies, huh?

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:43.360
From the looks of him, this fellow 
would be a Cephonodes hylas.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.450
A what?

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.570
It's a moth that looks a lot like a shrimp.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.650
A shrimp? How's that work?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.400
If causing trouble around here 
is against the rules...

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.440
You should get her under control.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:01.730
I hate that little bitch.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:04.590
The two of you are like two peas in a pod.

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:07.330
Hey, Tsuki, could you call a cleaner?

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.660
Feed him to the spiders.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:13.920
These people are no fun at all.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.940
Kuzuhara-san, do you like 
collecting insects?

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.210
Where's Hanakaze?

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.210
That was a joke, by the way.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.710
What's the mission?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.090
Ouch!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.140
You're preventing an assassination.

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:09.030
You're aware Yoshinobu-sama 
will be out tomorrow

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:12.100
to celebrate the completion 
of Tokyo Castle, right?

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.900
Janome...

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.030
The new wall has created a lot of support

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:22.900
among the rowdier crowds for 
the opposition, Kuchinawa.

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:28.170
Janome has been smuggling a variety 
of animals in from foreign countries.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.420
For new Changelings?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.920
Right. And we don't know what 
kind of power they'll have.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:39.190
They could pose a threat unlike 
anything we've seen before.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.770
<b>Construction on Tokyo Castle Complete 
Symbol of the Meiji-Tokugawa Regime</b>

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.370
Then Janome is going to be in control 
of these new Changelings,

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:49.820
and send them after Yoshinobu-sama?

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:53.810
There's not much time. Deal with this 
before it poses a threat to the festivities.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.900
Looks like the party's started already.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.200
Hanakaze.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.170
A little gift from a certain 
shrimp-looking moth bastard.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:04.330
A ledger of underworld deals, 
with clients listed.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:12.780
We can use this to track down 
where Janome's men are operating.

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:14.410
Tsukishiro.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:15.300
On it.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.480
Yukimura.

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:22.260
You know what I'm about to say?

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.060
I do.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:26.870
We exist in the shadows.

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:30.580
We owe our lives to the position 
granted to us by Yoshinobu-sama.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:31.670
But...

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:35.690
You are not allowed to run amok 
because of personal feelings.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:37.090
What do you suppose became 
of that fuss in Kyushu?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.470
Oh, the epidemic?

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.090
Yoshinobu-sama sent in a group of 
doctors and enacted a quarantine.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:56.860
I fell in love with those eyes, 
staring into the distance.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.970
How beautiful.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.420
It's a passage from your novel, Elena.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:06.720
"Don't Know Love." 
A wonderful piece of work.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:10.120
True enough. Not that I wrote 
a single word of it myself.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:10.870
Pardon?

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:15.060
I almost mistook you for an acanthus blossom, 
like those that bloom near the Mediterranean.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:17.730
Pardon us.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.790
He was actually pretty handsome...

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.610
And our target?

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:25.950
Him.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:31.140
On the surface, he's a retired senior exec 
from Yamagin Trading who provided the rich

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.170
with everything from steamships to lipstick,

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.650
and had his hands in all kinds of business.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:40.150
But beneath that facade, he's an old 
sack of shit who's big on smuggling.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:43.150
And from your reaction, 
he's resistant to seduction.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.390
The intel was good, though.

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:47.930
He'll be delivering the goods 
to Janome tonight.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:51.660
This is going to be a fun evening.

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:54.290
And the little bitch?

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.800
Otherwise occupied.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.920
Janome is meeting them here?

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.760
Come on, it's time.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:31.830
Why on earth would you do that?

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.080
The louder it is, the more fun it is.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.520
Wow!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.870
If they fly the coop on us...

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.070
It's over.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.680
You... evil little minx!

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:35.220
That is no way to talk to a lady.

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:43.260
Oh, finished already?

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:48.700
You're not big on mercy, are you?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.030
Do you think Janome might be handsome?

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.330
There's no one here to meet us.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.000
Are you sure this is the right place?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.910
It's supposed to be.

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:03.170
What is going on here?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.480
What the hell is this?

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.850
Contraband rice...

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:11.510
We were fed fake intel!

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.240
I thought so.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:21.860
Do you have any idea what just happened?

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.450
Oh, did I forget to tell you?

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:28.150
The town is full of hidden 
underground tunnels, like an ant hill.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:31.380
But there are only two points 
that exit near the castle:

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.780
one by the west gate, and one by the east.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:38.120
The western gate is out in the open 
and has a ton of security.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.710
And the tunnel that exits 
by the eastern gate?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.860
Sealed shut due to the 
tunnel crumbling with age.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:47.240
Not a path that any man could get through.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:48.220
But...

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.720
But what if you're not a man?

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:20.440
You, who would violate the foundation 
of what makes a man,

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:25.370
dwell now in the blue that surges within.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:04.370
I do not pity you.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.750
Nor do I hate you.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.750
But for the sake of my vengeance...

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:12.590
You must die.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:20.510
Yuki-chan?

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:28.050
M-Make it stop!

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.240
No!

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:48.630
<i>Why?</i>

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.100
<i>Amidst the pitiless white snow</i>

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.290
<i>A fleeting dream is scattered</i>

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:00.160
<i>The path back leads only to Hell</i>

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:02.640
<i>I have no regrets</i>

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:16.710
My name is Sawa.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:20.390
Sawa Karasumori.

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:24.390
<i>Sawa, look at me.</i>

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.910
I can't die yet.

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:31.300
Not until I have... revenge...

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.340
Wow!

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.930
<b>Tokyo Roster</b>

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.300
So she really is alive.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.020
<b>Tokyo Roster</b>

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:43.820
I can't wait to see that crow 
again. What do you say?

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.780
Sawa. Look at me, Sawa.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:20:01.180
This is important. No matter what you 
see or hear, you can't make a sound.

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:08.090
Don't leave me, Onii-chan!

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:14.980
Sawa... No matter what happens, 
you have to live.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.500
Survive, and live to see another day.
